# Backend API Routing Standards

## Versioned API Structure

* **Main API routes** (`routes/api.php`): Only unversioned routes like `/health`, `/version` and `/status`
* **Versioned API routes** (`routes/v1/api.php`, `routes/v2/api.php`, etc.): All business logic routes
* **Future-proofing**: All new API endpoints go in versioned routes, not main API

## Controller Organization

* **Base controllers**: `app/Http/Controllers/Api/` (e.g., `AuthController.php`)
* **Versioned controllers**: `app/Http/Controllers/Api/v1/`, `app/Http/Controllers/Api/v2/`, etc.
* **Versioned controllers extend base controllers** when possible for code reuse

## Route File Standards

### Main API (`routes/api.php`)
```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
use App\Http\Controllers\Api\v1\UtilityController;

// Unversioned API routes - only health and status for future proofing
Route::get('/health', [UtilityController::class, 'health']);

Route::middleware('debug.enabled')->group(function () {
    Route::get('/status', [UtilityController::class, 'status']);
});
```

### Versioned API (`routes/v1/api.php`, `routes/v2/api.php`, etc.)
```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;
use App\Http\Controllers\Api\v1\AuthController;  // EXPLICIT IMPORTS REQUIRED
use App\Http\Controllers\Api\v1\SomeController;  // NO AUTOMATIC NAMESPACE RESOLUTION

// Authentication routes
Route::prefix('auth')->group(function () {
    Route::post('/register', [AuthController::class, 'register']);
    Route::post('/login', [AuthController::class, 'login']);
    
    // Protected routes
    Route::middleware('auth:sanctum')->group(function () {
        Route::get('/user', [AuthController::class, 'user']);
        Route::post('/logout', [AuthController::class, 'logout']);
        Route::post('/logout-all', [AuthController::class, 'logoutAll']);
    });
});

```

## RouteServiceProvider Configuration

* **NO automatic namespace resolution** for versioned routes
* **Explicit imports required** in each versioned API file
* **RouteServiceProvider** only handles prefixing and middleware, not namespacing

```php
// RouteServiceProvider.php - mapVersionedApiRoutes()
Route::middleware('api')
    ->prefix("api/{$version}")
    ->group(function () use ($routeFile) {
        require $routeFile;  // NO namespace parameter
    });
```

## Controller Standards

### Base Controller Example
```php
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers\Api;

use App\Http\Controllers\Controller;
use Illuminate\Http\JsonResponse;

class AuthController extends Controller
{
    public function register(Request $request): JsonResponse
    {
        // Implementation
    }
    
    public function login(Request $request): JsonResponse
    {
        // Implementation
    }
}
```

### Versioned Controller Example
```php
<?php

namespace App\Http\Controllers\Api\v1;

use App\Http\Controllers\Api\AuthController as BaseAuthController;

class AuthController extends BaseAuthController
{
    // Extends base controller for code reuse
    // Can override methods if needed for v1-specific behavior
}
```

## Middleware Standards

* **Authentication**: `auth:sanctum` for protected routes
* **Permissions**: `permission:permission_name` for specific permissions
* **Roles**: `role:role_name` for specific roles
* **Role or Permission**: `role_or_permission:role|permission` for either/or

## Route Naming Conventions

* **Authentication**: `auth/register`, `auth/login`, `auth/user`, `auth/logout`
* **Business Logic**: Use descriptive names like `admin-panel`
* **Versioned URLs**: All business routes under `/api/v1/`, `/api/v2/`, etc.

## Do / Don't

* ✅ **DO** use explicit imports in versioned API files
* ✅ **DO** extend base controllers in versioned controllers
* ✅ **DO** keep main API routes minimal (health/status only)
* ✅ **DO** use descriptive route names and proper middleware
* ❌ **DON'T** rely on automatic namespace resolution
* ❌ **DON'T** put business logic in main API routes
* ❌ **DON'T** mix versioned and unversioned routes in same file

## Future API Versions

When creating v2, v3, etc.:
1. Create `routes/v2/api.php` with explicit imports
2. Create `app/Http/Controllers/Api/v2/` directory
3. Create versioned controllers that extend base controllers
4. RouteServiceProvider automatically picks up new versions

## Verification Checklist

1. Main API only has health/status routes
2. All business logic in versioned routes
3. Explicit imports in all versioned API files
4. Controllers properly namespaced and organized
5. Middleware applied correctly for auth/permissions/roles
6. RouteServiceProvider has no automatic namespace resolution
